Search complete. Four mailboxes, January 2011 through December 2013, full t=
ext including attachment contents. The results index is attached with messa=
ge identifiers, dates, parties and attachment names.<br />
<br />
Headline numbers. 241,700 messages matched the mailbox and date filters. 38=
 matched on the registrant name or the examination number. Twelve of those =
are the 2011 examination sequence, running from the notice of examination o=
n February 7, 2011 to the closing letter on June 28, 2011. One is from Octo=
ber 2013. The remaining 25 are unrelated traffic that mentions the firm in =
passing or matches on a transposed examination number.<br />
<br />
Recovered with the messages, as sent, with attachments intact:<br />
<br />
- The notice of examination and initial document request list, February 7, =
2011.<br />
- The preliminary findings memorandum, March 18, 2011, identifying the fee-=
debit authority as custody under Rule 206(4)-2 across 214 accounts.<br />
- The deficiency letter, April 20, 2011, six items, Item 4 being custody.<b=
r />
- The extension request of April 26 and the staff's grant of April 28.<br /=
>
- The firm's interim response, May 19, 2011, and the staff's position lette=
r of May 24.<br />
- An internal staff message of May 26 setting out what the staff intended t=
o require on Item 4.<br />
- A staff call memorandum dated June 1, 2011.<br />
- A letter from the firm's chief compliance officer dated June 2, 2011, wit=
h the signed original attached.<br />
- The examiner's closing recommendation of June 7 and the closing letter of=
 June 28, 2011.<br />
<br />
Terrence, read the June 2 letter first.<br />
